Long ago, in the Realm of Echoes, lived two spirits: Aethel, the Weaver of Light, and Thorne, the Keeper of Stones. They resided on separate peaks, divided by an abyss of starlight. The Great Creator decreed that they could only transcend their isolation by sharing their gifts. Each day, Aethel cast strands of golden silk across the void, trusting Thorne to catch them. If Thorne caught the silk and wove it into a bridge, the return was grand—a harvest of stardust that nourished them both. Yet, if Thorne greedily hoarded the silk, the bridge would collapse, and both would languish in darkness.

One cycle, Aethel sent everything she had, a bold act of faith. Thorne, standing at the precipice, felt the weight of the gift. He chose not to keep the silk for himself, but to weave it into a path of shimmering quartz. When the bridge solidified, the void vanished, and the two became one, their combined light illuminating the entire cosmos. They learned that the abyss was not a barrier, but a test of character. Hoarding led to solitude, while trust, returned with honor, birthed a golden age of prosperity and shared divinity.

